  "question": {
    "text": "During an adiabatic process, the pressure of a gas is found to be proportional to the cube of its absolute temperature. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mfrac></math> for the gas is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It is given that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>For an adiabatic process,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Assuming the gas to be a perfect gas, it can be written from equation (2) that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>P</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext></math></p><p>By comparing with equation(1), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>γ</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>γ</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}